{"1-4":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"joseph-h3130g","name":"Joseph","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's son","count":1,"firstVerse":4}],"places":[{"id":"beersheba-h0884","name":"Beersheba","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":3}],"words":[{"base":"H0595","lemma":"אָֽנֹכִ֫י","tr":"a·no·khi","gloss":"I","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":359},{"base":"H0884","lemma":"בְּאֵר שֶׁ֫בַע","tr":"be·er she·va","gloss":"Beersheba","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":68},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":350},{"base":"H3381","lemma":"יָרַד","tr":"ya·rad","gloss":"to go down","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":380},{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":641},{"base":"H4759","lemma":"מַרְאָה","tr":"mar·ah","gloss":"vision","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H5927","lemma":"עָלָה","tr":"a·lah","gloss":"to ascend: rise","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":889},{"base":"H7896","lemma":"שִׁית","tr":"shit","gloss":"to set: make","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":83},{"base":"H3327","lemma":"יִצְחָק","tr":"yits·chaq","gloss":"Isaac","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":108},{"base":"H2076","lemma":"זָבַח","tr":"za·vach","gloss":"to sacrifice","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":134}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I will make you into a great nation, and I will bless you; I will make your name great, so that you will be a blessing.","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"After these events, the word of the Lordcame to Abram in a vision: “Do not be afraid, Abram. I am your shield, your very great reward.”","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I have come down to rescue them from the hand of the Egyptians and to bring them up out of that land to a good and spacious land, a land flowing with milk and honey—the home of the Canaanites, Hittites, Amorites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites.","from":4},{"book":"DEU","chapter":26,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"and you are to declare before the LORD your God, “My father was a wandering Aramean, and he went down to Egypt few in number and lived there and became a great nation, mighty and numerous.","from":3},{"book":"JOB","chapter":33,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"For God speaks in one way and in another, yet no one notices.","from":2},{"book":"JOB","chapter":33,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"In a dream, in a vision in the night, when deep sleep falls upon men as they slumber on their beds,","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And Abraham planted a tamarisk tree in Beersheba, and there he called upon the name of the Lord, the Eternal God.","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"He moved on from there and dug another well, and they did not quarrel over it. He named it Rehoboth and said, “At last the Lordhas made room for us, and we will be fruitful in the land.”","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"5-7":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547h","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"places":[{"id":"beersheba-h0884","name":"Beersheba","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6}],"words":[{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":350},{"base":"H0884","lemma":"בְּאֵר שֶׁ֫בַע","tr":"be·er she·va","gloss":"Beersheba","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":68},{"base":"H0854","lemma":"אֵת","tr":"et","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":929},{"base":"H2233","lemma":"זֶ֫רַע","tr":"ze·ra","gloss":"seed","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":229},{"base":"H7408","lemma":"רָכַשׁ","tr":"ra·khash","gloss":"to gather","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H1323","lemma":"בַּת","tr":"bat","gloss":"daughter","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":588},{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":641},{"base":"H5375","lemma":"נָשָׂא","tr":"na·sa","gloss":"to lift: raise","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":656},{"base":"H5699","lemma":"עֲגָלָה","tr":"a·ga·lah","gloss":"cart","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":25},{"base":"H7399","lemma":"רְכוּשׁ","tr":"re·khush","gloss":"property","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":28}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":45,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"You are also directed to tell them: ‘Take wagons from the land of Egypt for your young children and your wives, and bring your father and come back.","from":5},{"book":"GEN","chapter":45,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So the sons of Israel did as they were told. Joseph gave them wagons as Pharaoh had instructed, and he also gave them provisions for their journey.","from":5},{"book":"JOS","chapter":24,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and to Isaac I gave Jacob and Esau. I gave Esau Mount Seir to possess, but Jacob and his sons went down to Egypt.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":105,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then Israel entered Egypt; Jacob dwelt in the land of Ham.","from":6},{"book":"ISA","chapter":52,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"For this is what the Lord GOD says: “At first My people went down to Egypt to live, then Assyria oppressed them without cause.","from":6},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So Jacob went down to Egypt, where he and our fathers died.","from":6},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the Lordsaid to Abram, “Know for certain that your descendants will be strangers in a land that is not their own, and they will be enslaved and mistreated four hundred years.","from":6},{"book":"GEN","chapter":31,"verse":17,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Jacob got up and put his children and his wives on camels, and he drove all his livestock before him, along with all the possessions he had acquired in Paddan-aram, to go to his father Isaac in the land in Canaan.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"8-15":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"carmi-h3756g","name":"Carmi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Reuben","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"hanoch-h2585j","name":"Hanoch","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Reuben","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"hezron-h2696g","name":"Hezron","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Reuben","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"pallu-h6396","name":"Pallu","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Reuben","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"a-wife-of-simeon-h8095i","name":"a wife of Simeon","kind":"person","brief":"From Simeon","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"canaanite-woman-h3669g","name":"Canaanite woman","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"jachin-h3199g","name":"Jachin","kind":"person","brief