:"Then Joseph sent for his father Jacob and all his relatives, seventy-five in all.","from":27},{"book":"GEN","chapter":29,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Since Jacob loved Rachel, he answered, “I will serve you seven years for your younger daughter Rachel.”","from":19},{"book":"GEN","chapter":29,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Laban gave his servant girl Zilpah to his daughter Leah as her maidservant.","from":18}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":12}]},"28-34":{"people":[{"id":"joseph-h3130g","name":"Joseph","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's son","count":4,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547h","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":2,"firstVerse":31}],"places":[{"id":"goshen-h1657g","name":"Goshen","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34}],"words":[{"base":"H1657","lemma":"גֹּ֫שֶׁן","tr":"go·shen","gloss":"Goshen","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":15},{"base":"H3130","lemma":"יוֹסֵף","tr":"yo·seph","gloss":"Joseph","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":213},{"base":"H6629","lemma":"צֹאן","tr":"tson","gloss":"flock","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":274},{"base":"H6677","lemma":"צַוָּאר","tr":"tsav·var","gloss":"neck","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":42},{"base":"H0582","lemma":"אֱנוֹשׁ","tr":"e·nosh","gloss":"human","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":565},{"base":"H4735","lemma":"מִקְנֶה","tr":"miq·neh","gloss":"livestock","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":76},{"base":"H7462","lemma":"בֵּית־עֵ֫קֶד הָרֹעִים","tr":"bet-e·qed ha·ro·im","gloss":"House of Shepherds","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":175},{"base":"H6547","lemma":"פַּרְעֹה","tr":"par·oh","gloss":"Pharaoh","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":274},{"base":"H5750","lemma":"עוֹד","tr":"od","gloss":"still","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":490},{"base":"H0251","lemma":"אָח","tr":"ach","gloss":"brother: male-sibling","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":629}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LUK","chapter":2,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"“Sovereign Lord, as You have promised, You now dismiss Your servant in peace.","from":30},{"book":"LUK","chapter":2,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"For my eyes have seen Your salvation,","from":30},{"book":"GEN","chapter":45,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"“Enough!” declared Israel. “My son Joseph is still alive! I will go to see him before I die.”","from":30},{"book":"GEN","chapter":45,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"You shall settle in the land of Goshen and be near me—you and your children and grandchildren, your flocks and herds, and everything you own.","from":28},{"book":"EXO","chapter":8,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But Moses replied, “It would not be right to do that, because the sacrifices we offer to the LORD our God would be detestable to the Egyptians. If we offer sacrifices that are detestable before the Egyptians, will they not stone us?","from":34},{"book":"GEN","chapter":4,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Later she gave birth to Cainʼs brother Abel. Now Abel was a keeper of sheep, while Cain was a tiller of the soil.","from":32},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now Noah, a man of the soil, proceeded to plant a vineyard.","from":32},{"book":"GEN","chapter":30,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"That very day Laban removed all the streaked or spotted male goats and every speckled or spotted female goat—every one that had any white on it—and every dark-colored lamb, and he placed them under the care of his sons.","from":34}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]}}